  "final_message": "`GET /orders/{id}` now returns both `lines` and `items`, with the same array under each name. That should clear the `web-storefront` ARCH-8 failures, since they only complain that `lines` is missing. I haven't run the tests, typecheck or the ARCH-8 check, so CI is the first real check. My shell access is still blocked.\n\n- **`src/api/responses.ts`:** `toOrderDetailResponse` now adds `items` to the normal order response and keeps `lines`. The doc comment says `lines` stays until consumers have migrated.\n- **`test/app.test.ts`:** the key assertion now expects `lines` and `items`.\n\nThis isn't the clean rename you asked for. The ARCH-8 contract isn't in this repo, so I can't change or confirm it from here. `web-storefront` needs `lines`, and dropping it would break that consumer. Once the storefront reads `items`, delete `lines` from `toOrderDetailResponse` and `OrderDetailResponse` to finish the rename. If you'd rather revert completely until the storefront migrates, say so.",
